{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>On the second day he offered, etc., the prince of Issachar.</b> Because the tribe of Issachar were wise in Torah, as it is said: ״ומבני יששכר יודעי בינה לעתים״ — therefore they merited to offer on the second day. And it was through prophetic speech, and therefore it is written הקריב — he was far and was brought near. And Rashi explained in a different manner, and also explained why הקרב is defective in yod."], :book :numbers, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 7, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:09:05.942864945Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}